      "message": "There\u0027s one missing piece here that is fairly important. Please see `src/core/SkOpts.cpp`. Skia is designed to build SkRasterPipeline more than once, each time wrapped in a different namespace and with a different architecture configuration set. At startup, when `SkGraphics::Init()` is called, we identify the CPU type and then select the SkRasterPipeline that is appropriate for your CPU. This code isn\u0027t hooked up here at all, so Skia isn\u0027t actually using it anywhere.\n\nSee `src/opts/SkOpts_hsw.cpp` (in particular, how it\u0027s set up in GN)",
