      "writtenOn": "2023-11-16T17:40:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Isn\u0027t the right implementation actually:\n```\n    __mmask16 mask64 \u003d _mm512_test_epi32_mask(c, c);\n    return mask64 \u003d 0xffff;\n````\n\nWe need to ensure that each 32-bit lane in c contains a non-zero value. (They will happen to each be ~0 if they are non-zero, but that doesn\u0027t matter). We can\u0027t use epi64, because we\u0027d incorrectly ignore a zero lane adjacent to a non-zero lane. And then we need to make sure the mask contains ALL the bits set.",
